# Save files are captured bytes, not source text.
#
# This repository is cloned with core.autocrlf=true on Windows, which rewrites the
# line endings of anything Git considers text. Assets/Tests/Fixtures/*.sav is a save
# file written by a shipped player and kept as evidence of what an older save format
# actually looked like (see that folder's README). A save is validated by a checksum
# over its payload, and its whole value here is being byte-for-byte what the player
# wrote -- so it must never be normalised, reformatted or converted on checkout.
#
# Marking it binary is the only way to say that to Git. Deliberately scoped to save
# files alone: adding rules for Unity's YAML scenes and assets would renormalise
# every one of them across the whole history, which is a separate change.
*.sav binary
